## Task 3 — litestream wiring (with one self-inflicted bug, fixed)
Backup: /etc/litestream.yml.bak-livefire-20261017 (kept for restore step).
First append used an UNQUOTED heredoc through ssh: local bash expanded
${LITESTREAM_S3_*} to empty, sidecar logged S3 credential errors for the
three new DBs only (pilot legs stayed ok — blast radius zero). Diagnosed via
journalctl, restored the backup, re-appended via stdin redirect so the
${...} references survive literally (verified: 5 entries with
LITESTREAM_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID). Durable rule: never pass ${...} through an
unquoted heredoc to a remote host — push bytes via stdin redirect.
After restart + 60s:
```
/var/lib/dg/verify_probe.sqlite       ok  txid 01
/var/lib/dg/billing_dev_pilot.sqlite  ok  txid 02
/var/lib/dg/pet_todo_live.sqlite      ok  txid 01
/var/lib/dg/pet_board_live.sqlite     ok  txid 02
/var/lib/dg/pet_events_live.sqlite    ok  txid 02
```

